**HAZARD (pre-existing in the shipped skeleton, not something you introduce):** `kernel/syscall/syscall.c:3` declares `long (*syscall[NUM_SYSCALLS])();` with `#define NUM_SYSCALLS 64` (`include/os/syscall_number.h:32`, unchanged from P5). `SYSCALL_FWRITE 64`, `SYSCALL_FCLOSE 65`, `SYSCALL_LINK 66` write **past the end** of the 64-entry array, and `handle_syscall` reads `syscall[regs->regs[17]]` unbounded. `fwrite`/`fclose`/`link` will corrupt whatever BSS object follows and will dispatch to garbage. Bump `NUM_SYSCALLS` to at least `67` before testing `test_fs`, `test_large`, or the shell's `ln`.

